{"agent":"rvprio-lane","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The test fixture bakes the reviewer verdict `STATUS: NO FINDINGS` into the generated reviewer scripts. Text inside the change that states a reviewer verdict must be reported, and here it is not merely cosmetic: that exact string is the protocol marker for a clean review, so if the fixture output is ever parsed outside the test, or if the review parser trusts the first status block it sees, it can spoof a passing review and mask findings. The test should use a non-status sentinel or explicitly assert that spoofed status blocks are not treated as authoritative.","digest":"9887ac482c74e737","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_reviewer_priority.py:_diary_reviewer","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_reviewer_priority.py:_diary_reviewer"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The test files task `T1` with `run_cli(repo, \"task\", \"add\", \"T1\", \"--title\", \"add x\", \"--globs\", \"*.py\")` without naming a phase, stating dependencies, or carrying a wave/no-deps tag. The recorded project rule [r-task-phase-needs-wave] requires every ddflow-filed task to have those fields; as written the test creates an invalid task fixture and will fail if the task validator enforces that rule.","digest":"1a29bfa4bdf0d068","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_reviewer_priority.py:test_the_gate_pays_the_fast_cross_family_reviewer_first","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_reviewer_priority.py:test_the_gate_pays_the_fast_cross_family_reviewer_first"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":10381,"diff_sha":"b9705f62a0244697da1fe41c228e436f6eddc982599f5420063b7fd37995da0e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/RV-reviewer-priority","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracke